    "created_at": "2016-08-16T15:54:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-16T15:54:25Z",
    "body": "All APIs that take `Node` should throw when passed an `Attr`, IMO. Don't care much about which exception; some may historically have been defined as throwing `InvalidNodeTypeError` or `HierarchyRequestError` or something.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
